{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-19T12:32:18.951Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"594846e624993d8c433f6429","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-19T12:32:18.951Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-19T12:32:18.951Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Plan for bisect: single command 'pm vcs bisect' with start|good|bad|skip|run|status|reset subcommands. Durable session state lives in the worktree's private control directory (atomic write) so a crash mid-walk leaves a resumable session; session milestones (start, conclusion, reset) are appended to PM history as comments on the linked item, so concurrent agents see each other's sessions and append-only history is never clobbered. Candidates are ordered oldest-first by ancestry; outcomes are keyed by stable change identity so rewritten commit ids (rebase/amend/describe) reuse recorded results. Linked test execution reuses the pm SDK runTest (pm test --run semantics). Outcomes: good, bad, skip (manual), untestable (spawn/timeout/signal/empty), conflicted (candidate carries unresolved conflict units). Original branch and commit are restored after success, refusal, SIGINT and crash-resume."}]}],"before_hash":"f4fd3a2f1e93ad654998e0677419c21e6378c13e001bff9581daf11941fb6d92","after_hash":"ffd7e375636382d3339c600f089aaa01b43790040dd285f12137e89d990e7c7f","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8022cca73b2ece59b99d59263a7b237bf537cb3b519955decdfb6fcaba242b07"}
